rsquo;s 5 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 38 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 that same middle saw September to October at 35% of normal and November to December at 47%. So far in 2026 it shows March to April at 29% and May to June at 222%. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, with grid 13989 at 52% of normal.</p>"}
